@description REAPER MCP — Model Context Protocol interface (immersive/spatial audio)
@version 1.14.0
@author James Livingston
@link https://github.com/inseglet-audio/inseglet
@provides
  [darwin] reaper_mcp.dylib https://github.com/inseglet-audio/inseglet/releases/download/v$version/reaper_mcp.dylib
@changelog
  Fourteen more tools say what they adjusted, and one had nothing to say.

  1.13.3 gave `track.set_channels` a `clamped` flag and a `warnings` line. Fourteen more mutating
  tools carry it now, declared in each tool's output schema and listed as required.

  NINE INPUT CLAMPERS -- transport.set_playrate, track.set_rec_mon, track.set_rec_mode,
  track.set_folder, item.set_position, item.set_length, item.set_fade_in, item.set_fade_out,
  take.set_pan -- name what was ASKED and what was USED. The comparison is against the caller's own
  value, never an intermediate, so a value adjusted twice reports the distance it travelled.

  FIVE PER-NOTE PINS -- midi.apply_groove, humanize, nudge, quantize, stretch -- report a COUNT.
  They do not adjust an input: the argument is honoured exactly and some notes still cannot land
  where it implies, so they pin to the item start. "Requested X, used Y" would be false for these.

  Nothing about any adjustment itself changed. This release changes what callers are TOLD, not what
  REAPER is given. `required` grows on fourteen tools, which is why this is a minor bump.

  spatial.set_source_position was examined and deliberately left alone: it was listed among the
  silent adjusters and is not one -- the construct behind that listing is an FX-index lookup
  fallback. The declared bounds are still not enforced; a tool tells you it clamped your value, it
  does not refuse it.

  Surface 190 tools / 4 resources / 5 prompts -- UNMOVED. ctest 29 -> 30, one added.
